WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
Hi, I'm Briana from freeCodeCamp

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.900
and today we're going to talk 
about the basics of computer hardware.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.800
Computers are made up 
of four basic parts:

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.180
The Input/Output, CPU, 
and Memory.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:14.460
The Input is what you're 
putting into the computer.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.100
Think about mouse, keyboard, 
microphone,

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.660
any way you're getting 
data into the computer.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.200
The Output is what you're 
watching on your monitor

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.200
or listening to on 
your speakers.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.180
These can both be any format 
like text, numbers,

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.840
videos, images, what-have-you. 
It doesn't matter.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:35.380
The CPU stands for 
Central Processing Unit

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.840
and that's what we all think of 
when we think of a computer.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.920
It's what does the functions.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.360
It's what runs the software.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.040
It manipulates the data.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:46.580
The Memory is where we 
store data and information.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.820
Now the CPU has exclusive 
access to this memory.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.800
You can't get to the Memory 
from the Input

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.580
or from the Output 
without the use of the CPU.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:58.120
So just to review we've got 
four basic parts of a computer:

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:03.180
the Input/Output, 
CPU, and Memory.

